        <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
          <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-heading font-bold mb-8 text-slate-900">
            Lab containers for Munich: what föhn, the gravel plain and southern Germany’s densest research cluster demand of the engineering
          </h2>
          <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none text-gray-700 space-y-6">
            <p>
              <strong>Munich and its hinterland are southern Germany’s densest research and pharma cluster.</strong> In a tight space, universities with their university hospitals on the Isar and in Großhadern, research centres in Neuherberg, biomedical research institutes in Martinsried, a research reactor with neutron source in Garching, the Martinsried-Planegg biotech cluster with more than 50 companies, the Penzberg pharma site, plus aerospace and defence technology in Ottobrunn and an automotive research and innovation centre all compete. Anyone ordering a container laboratory here is not ordering a standard product — they are ordering site intelligence for a region with its own laws of nature.
            </p>
            <p>
              <strong>We know this market in detail.</strong> We know that föhn at the Alpine fringe challenges HVAC controls that are never tested in Hamburg or Berlin. We know that the Munich gravel plain of Würm-period gravel, soil class 4 to 5 to DIN 18196, is bearing but still demands a raft foundation with uplift protection because of groundwater fluctuation. We know that large-scale research in Garching requires vibration tolerances below 1 µm/s, and that the Martinsried biotech cluster expects safety standards that, in a building application, demand different safety concepts from a normal S2 laboratory. These details are not in the quotation — they are the engineering foundation of every container that leaves our Albstadt works.
            </p>
            <p>
              <strong>Made in Albstadt, turnkey in Munich.</strong> Final assembly and interior fit-out are carried out with Wesemann furniture at our own works — a factory visit can be planned at any time. Via the A8 the heavy-goods distance is only around 280 kilometres; via the A99 Munich orbital all Munich research, hospital and pharma sites are directly reachable. That is the shortest delivery distance from our works into the DACH metropolises — one transport day, not a week-long project.
            </p>
            <p>
              Whether you need a <strong>mobile laboratory Munich</strong> for a time-limited project at the Großhadern university hospital, a <strong>modular lab container Munich</strong> for a permanent expansion in the Martinsried biotech cluster, or a <strong>container laboratory Munich</strong> with BSL-3 for infection research — we deliver all three answers from the same platform: the LABtoGO from our Albstadt works.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ANWENDUNGSBEREICHE MÜNCHEN -->
