              <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">The Bavarian Building Code (Bayerische Bauordnung, BayBO) is decisive. Inside the city boundary the Munich Local Building Commission reviews centrally — uniformly for all 25 city districts. Outside, the rural district offices of Munich, Starnberg, Weilheim-Schongau, Ebersberg or Fürstenfeldbruck review under BayBO — each with its own practice. We submit review-ready building documents matched to the authority’s practice.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">LGL Bayern – BSL-3 and GenTG notification</h3>
              <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">BSL-3 in Bavaria requires a permit under BioStoffV (federal law) plus a notification to LGL Bayern — the Bavarian State Office for Health and Food Safety, Biological Safety unit. For genetic-engineering facilities S1/S2/S3 an additional notification under GenTG is required. We supply the risk assessment, safety concept and complete application documents.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">Hospital siting</h3>
              <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">Siting at the university hospitals on the Isar or in Großhadern is coordinated with the Bavarian State Building Office Munich and the hospital building office. Fire-protection concept under BayBO plus hospital-building-ordinance practice, sterile logistics and alignment with the Munich fire directorate (Branddirektion München).</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">Radiation protection Garching</h3>
              <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">Siting near a reactor or beam-diagnostics facility requires coordination with the radiation-protection authority and, where applicable, additional notifications under the Radiation Protection Ordinance. We supply lead-lined modules and radiation-protection documentation on request.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

